Changes made (2026-10-01):

1. In both files, the state "Schedule Follow Up III": the conditional_transition that assigned Stage I, II, III or IV
   from the attribute lung_cancer_nondiagnosis_counter (<= 36, <= 72, <= 108 months, otherwise IV) was replaced by a
   distributed_transition with Stage I 0.2002, Stage II 0.0841, Stage III 0.1982 and Stage IV 0.5175. These are the
   SEER 17 non-small cell lung cancer stage-at-diagnosis shares (20.0, 8.4, 19.8 and 51.7 percent; diagnosed
   2010-2015, age 50+, first primary, known stage), scaled proportionally to sum to 1. Remarks explaining the change
   and its source were added to that state. See docs/synthea-stage-patch.md in this repository for the reason.
2. The files were re-serialized as JSON by a script, so whitespace and formatting differ from upstream beyond the
   change above. No other state was edited.
